Package: ratioPCR
Title: Ratiometric Quantification of Co-Amplified PCR Templates
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jochen", "Kinter", email = "j.kinter@unibas.ch",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Adeline", "Stiefvater", role = "aut"),
    person("Samira", "Osterop", role = "aut"),
    person("Michael", "Sinnreich", role = "aut"))
Description: Quantifies the relative abundance of templates that are amplified
    together in a single real-time PCR reaction. The amplification bias between
    templates is estimated from calibration reactions of known composition and
    corrected with a mechanistic model of the amplification process, so that a
    measured fluorescence ratio can be converted into a template ratio.
    Provides import of instrument export files, baseline and efficiency
    estimation, calibration fitting with quality control, forward and inverse
    ratio estimation with batch processing, simulation of amplification curves,
    and plotting helpers for calibration and results.
